To add the ability to mark a to-do item as completed, you'll need to update the state structure to include a `completed` property for each to-do item, and then create a function to toggle the completed status.

Follow these steps to implement this functionality:

1. Update the `addTodo` function in `App.js`:

Modify the `addTodo` function to include a `completed` property, initially set to `false`, for each new to-do item:


```javascript
const addTodo = (text) => {
 setTodos([...todos, { text, completed: false }]);
};
```
1. Create a `toggleCompleted` function in `App.js`:

Add a new function called `toggleCompleted` that takes an index as its argument and updates the `completed` property of the corresponding to-do item in the state:


```javascript
const toggleCompleted = (index) => {
 setTodos(
 todos.map((todo, i) =>
 i === index ? { ...todo, completed: !todo.completed } : todo
 )
 );
};
```
1. Pass the `toggleCompleted` function to the `TodoList` component:

Update the `TodoList` component in `App.js` to receive the `toggleCompleted` function as a prop:


```javascript
<TodoList todos={todos} onToggleCompleted={toggleCompleted} />
```
1. Pass the `onToggleCompleted` prop from `TodoList` to `TodoItem`:

In `TodoList.js`, pass the `onToggleCompleted` prop to the `TodoItem` component:


```javascript
const TodoList = ({ todos, onToggleCompleted }) => {
 return (
 <ul className="list-group">
 {todos.map((todo, index) => (
 <TodoItem
 key={index}
 index={index}
 todo={todo}
 onToggleCompleted={onToggleCompleted}
 />
 ))}
 </ul>
 );
};
```
1. Update the `TodoItem` component:

In `TodoItem.js`, add an `onClick` event listener to the list item that calls the `onToggleCompleted` function with the item's index. Additionally, apply a CSS class to visually indicate the completed status:


```javascript
import React from 'react';

const TodoItem = ({ index, todo, onToggleCompleted }) => {
 return (
 <li
 className={`list-group-item${todo.completed ? ' text-decoration-line-through' : ''}`}
 onClick={() => onToggleCompleted(index)}
 style={{ cursor: 'pointer' }}
 >
 {todo.text}
 </li>
 );
};

export default TodoItem;
```
Now, when you click a to-do item in your list, it will be marked as completed with a line-through text decoration, and its `completed` property in the state will be updated accordingly. Clicking the item again will toggle the completed status back to false.
